### FilmFuse core-api - ratings (quick rate / review). Token: see me.http.
# One row per (user, movie); re-rating overwrites it. Every write marks the taste vector dirty.
# A movie not yet cached is fetched from the catalog (404 if the catalog does not know it).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@token = paste-access-token-here
@movieId = 603

### Quick rate (defaults: visibility FRIENDS, source QUICK_RATE)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ratings/{{movieId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"score": 8}

### Review: a note (<= 1000 chars), spoilers flag, visibility, watch date
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ratings/{{movieId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "score": 9,
  "body": "Still holds up.",
  "containsSpoilers": false,
  "visibility": "PUBLIC",
  "watchedOn": "2026-10-15",
  "source": "POST_WATCH"
}

### My rating of one movie (404 if none)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/ratings/{{movieId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### All my ratings, newest first (pass nextCursor as ?cursor=)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/ratings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Remove (204, idempotent)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ratings/{{movieId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Score out of range -> 400 (fieldErrors.score)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ratings/{{movieId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"score": 11}

### ONBOARDING_SWIPE is only for /me/ratings/batch -> 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ratings/{{movieId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"score": 5, "source": "ONBOARDING_SWIPE"}
